esents Rumi's startling conviction that \"Love is the strongest unifying\r\n \r\nforce in the Universe.\" Rumi said that everything in the universe is in orbit. \r\nThe atoms, molecules, galaxies, and universes are all turning, around a center, \r\nand the center is Love. For Rumi, peace is the natural quest of a 'whole person', \r\nand the perimeters between self and universe are mitigated to the extent \r\nthat the material body becomes indistinct of its typical cultural identity.\r\n\r\n \r\nOffering a unique look at Being and Oneness, Rumi's poetry redefines \r\n'Wholeness' with deep spiritual knowledge, intellectual acumen, wit, humor, \r\nand literary genius. As one admirer said, \"In the fight to root out conflict, \r\nviolence and war, Rumi's holistic view of unconditional love may prove one \r\nof our best friends.\""},"weight":"1 pounds","covers":[7151849],"physical_format":"Hardcover","lc_classifications":["PK6482 .A84 2012","PK6482.A84 2012"],"key":"/books/OL25379825M","publish_places":["USA"],"pagination":"xxix, 148","source_records":["amazon:1930337663","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part40.utf8:174894911:2005","bwb:9781930337664","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-021.mrc:89157795:2044","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:695110383:2036","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_012.bib.mrc:121675421:3468"],"title":"Rumi's Holistic Humanism: The Timeless Appeal of the Great Mystic Poet","lccn":["2012904407"],"number_of_pages":180,"isbn_10":["1930337663"],"publish_date":"July 2012","works":[{"key":"/works/OL16708002W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9 x 6 x 3/4 inches","oclc_numbers":["805655109"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2012-07-19T13:46:55.184058"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-08-01T12:51:34.074906"}}},"ISBN:9780195369236":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780195369236","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25383020M/Beyond_dogma","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/beyonddogmarumis0000moja","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9305855-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Oxford University Press"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Note on the text","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Introduction","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"1. The sources","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"2. Friendship with God in relation to prophethood","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"3. Divine communication","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"4. The friend of God and the Shariah","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"5. The friend of God and miracles","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Conclusion","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Notes","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Bibliography","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Index.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"covers":[9305855],"local_id":["urn:mgc:31927002085808","urn:cst:10017031479"],"full_title":"Beyond dogma Rumi's teachings on friendship with God and early Sufi theories","lc_classifications":["PK6482 .M65 2012","PK6482.M65 2012"],"key":"/books/OL25383020M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL5187305A","name":"J. A. Mojaddedi"}],"ocaid":"beyonddogmarumis0000moja","publish_places":["Oxford","New York"],"subtitle":"Rumi's teachings on friendship with God and early Sufi theories","isbn_13":["9780195369236"],"pagination":"214 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i30.records.utf8:11018077:1110","marc:marc_marygrove/marygrovecollegelibrary.full.D20191108.T213022.internetarchive2nd_REPACK.mrc:190753747:4225","ia:beyonddogmarumis0000moja","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:87691173:4162","bwb:9780195369236","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part38.utf8:196090732:1110","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:87743420:4162","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:396338963:3118","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-021.mrc:72230309:1301","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_027.bib.mrc:184683386:3823"],"title":"Beyond dogma","lccn":["2011029081"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [197]-203) and index."},"number_of_pages":214,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["297.4092"],"subjects":["Sufism","Criticism and interpretation","Knowableness","God (Islam)"],"subject_people":["Jalāl al-Dīn Rūmī Maulana (1207-1273)"],"publish_country":"uk ","publish_date":"2012","by_statement":"by Jawid Mojaddedi","works":[{"key":"/works/OL16713094W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["743298784"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Despite Rumi's (d. 1273) recent emergence as a best-selling poet in the English-speaking world, fundamental questions about his teachings, such as the relationship of his Sufi mysticism to the wider Islamic religion, remain contested. In this groundbreaking study, Jawid Mojaddedi reaches to the heart of the matter by examining Rumi's teachings on walaya (Friendship with God) in light of earlier discourse in the wider Sufi tradition and juridico-theological Islam. Walaya is not only central to Rumi's teachings, but forms the basis for the celebration of intimacy, communication with the Divine, and transcendence of conventional religiosity in his poetry. And yet walaya is the aspect of Sufism which has proven the most difficult to reconcile with juridico-theological Islam. In addition to its focus on Rumi, Beyond Dogma presents a perceptive analysis of the historical development of the discourse on walaya in the formative centuries of Sufism. This period coincides with the time when juridico-theological Islam rose to dominance, as reflected in the harmonizing efforts of theoretical Sufi writings, especially the manuals of the tenth and eleventh centuries. Mojaddedi's analysis facilitates a nuanced and contextualized evaluation of Rumi's teachings on walaya, which had already attracted a range of views before his time: from arguments in favor of its superiority to Prophethood, to guarantees of subordinate deference towards the Prophetic heritage interpreted by juridico-theological scholars. In the process, Beyond Dogma enables a fresh evaluation of the influential early Sufi manuals in their historical context, while also highlighting the significance for juridico-theological scholars of fundamental dogma in the process of consolidating their own dominance."},"latest_revision":11,"revision":11,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2012-07-25T11:46:50.146055"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-01-16T16:27:57.012063"}}},"ISBN:9781453833100":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781453833100","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL54552895M/Spiritual_Rumi","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL54552895M/Spiritual_Rumi","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL9807058A","name":"Jalal Rumi"}],"isbn_13":["9781453833100"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"number_of_pages":192,"publish_date":"2010","publishers":["CreateSpace Independent Publishing Platform"],"source_records":["bwb:9781453833100"],"subjects":["Jalal al-din rumi, maulana, 1207-1273","Persian poetry, translations into english"],"title":"Spiritual Rumi","weight":"0.350","works":[{"key":"/works/OL40081667W"}],"key":"/books/OL54552895M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-09-21T23:22:46.1